      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mangham, a village in Richland Parish, sits in northeastern Louisiana, known for its tight‑knit community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangham%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1890, Mangham grew around a railroad stop that connected the region to larger markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangham%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community straddles the border with Franklin Parish, giving it a unique position between two parishes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangham%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mangham publishes the Richland Beacon‑News, a weekly newspaper that serves Rayville, the seat of Richland Parish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangham%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Three schools serve Mangham: an elementary, a junior high, and a high school covering grades PK‑12.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangham%2C_Louisiana"
    },
